      "expectation": "needs_review once per control whose computed style does not change when it\nreceives focus in a way that can serve as an indicator\n(Layout::focus_visible, measured by accessibility::probes): no new or changed\noutline, box-shadow, border, background, text colour or text decoration, and\nno browser focus ring. The browser's own focus ring, an author outline, a\nbackground change and a shadow each count as an indicator. A control that\ncannot take focus, or that is not reachable with Tab (tabindex=-1), is not a\ncandidate. Transitions are suspended during the measurement so a transition\non the focus style does not hide the change. Review, not violation: whether\nthe change is perceivable is a human judgement. A page whose scripts break the\nprobe records the rule as not run (CapabilityMissing).",
      "method": "shared",
      "capabilities": [
        "dom",
        "computed_style",
        "interaction"
      ],
      "page_level": false,
